     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Hello all,<br><br>I cant figure out how to get the predict function to give me values in the original units. Here is my coding:<br><br><br> a&lt;-read.csv(&quot;BEVI2012_20m.csv&quot;)<br> y&lt;-a[,2:21]<br> R&lt;-202<br> T&lt;-4<br>crp&lt;-scale(a[25])<br>forest&lt;- scale(a[23])<br>patch&lt;-scale(a[24])<br> db&lt;-c(0,20,40,60,80,100)<br> <br> site.Covs&lt;-data.frame(cp=a[22], crp, forest, patch)<br><br>beviumf&lt;-unmarkedFrameGDS(y=y, siteCovs=site.Covs, survey=&quot;point&quot;, dist.breaks=db,unitsIn=&quot;m&quot;, numPrimary=T)<br>summary(beviumf)<br><br><br><br>BEVI&lt;-list()<br><br>BEVInull&lt;-gdistsamp(~1, ~1, ~1, beviumf, keyfun=&quot;halfnorm&quot;,output=&quot;density&quot;, unitsOut=&quot;ha&quot;,mixture=&quot;NB&quot;, K=50)<br>BEVIcp&lt;-gdistsamp(~cp, ~1, ~1, beviumf,keyfun=&quot;halfnorm&quot;, output=&quot;density&quot;, unitsOut=&quot;ha&quot;, mixture=&quot;NB&quot;, K=50)<br>BEVIcrp&lt;-gdistsamp(~crp, ~1, ~1, beviumf,keyfun=&quot;halfnorm&quot;, output=&quot;density&quot;, unitsOut=&quot;ha&quot;, mixture=&quot;NB&quot;, K=50)<br>BEVIforest&lt;-gdistsamp(~forest, ~1, ~1, beviumf,keyfun=&quot;halfnorm&quot;, output=&quot;density&quot;, unitsOut=&quot;ha&quot;, mixture=&quot;NB&quot;, K=50)<br>BEVIpatch&lt;-gdistsamp(~patch, ~1, ~1, beviumf,keyfun=&quot;halfnorm&quot;,output=&quot;density&quot;, unitsOut=&quot;ha&quot;, mixture=&quot;NB&quot;, K=50)<br>BEVIpatchsq&lt;-gdistsamp(~(patch)^2, ~1, ~1, beviumf,keyfun=&quot;halfnorm&quot;,output=&quot;density&quot;, unitsOut=&quot;ha&quot;, mixture=&quot;NB&quot;, K=50)<br>BEVIforestcp&lt;-gdistsamp(~forest+cp, ~1, ~1, beviumf,keyfun=&quot;halfnorm&quot;,output=&quot;density&quot;, unitsOut=&quot;ha&quot;, mixture=&quot;NB&quot;, K=50)<br>BEVIforestcrp&lt;-gdistsamp(~forest+crp, ~1, ~1, beviumf,keyfun=&quot;halfnorm&quot;,output=&quot;density&quot;, unitsOut=&quot;ha&quot;, mixture=&quot;NB&quot;, K=50)<br>BEVIforestpatch&lt;-gdistsamp(~forest+patch, ~1, ~1, beviumf,keyfun=