   "id": "4quq_FuDBQAJ",
   "from": "Dan Linden",
   "author": "527d9b3ec7deff2d",
   "date": "2015-12-18T15:11:35Z",
   "subject": "Re: Problems with predict in unmarkedFrameGDS",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Well, you&#39;d be amazed how often people resolve problems with a bit of troubleshooting on their part.<br><br>Your new data frame is incorrect for 2 reasons: 1) the forest covariate in the BEVI data file ranges from 0 to 1, not 0 to 100; and 2) regardless, you fit the abundance relationship with the scaled covariate so new model predictions need that covariate to be scaled.  The new data frame needs values for forest that look something like:<br><br><span style=\"font-family:courier new,monospace\">new.forest.s &lt;- seq(range(forest)[1],range(forest)[2],length=100)</span><br><br>And if you want that translated back into actual forest proportion values, you need to use the mean and standard deviation from the scaled forest vector:<br><br><span style=\"font-family:courier new,monospace\">new.forest &lt;- new.forest.s*attr(forest,&quot;scaled:scale&quot;)+attr(forest,&quot;scaled:center&quot;)</span><br></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
